### Steel Store — manual smoke requests
### Usage (JetBrains HTTP client):
###   1. Run the "Login" request — `{{token}}` is captured from the response.
###   2. Run any subsequent request — it auto-attaches the Bearer header.
### Or use IntelliJ / VSCode REST Client extensions.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login (captures token)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

> {%
client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### List products
GET {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search products by name
GET {{host}}/api/products?name=thép
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### Create product
# @name createProduct
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Thép phi 6",
  "unit": "kg",
  "currentImportPrice": 18000,
  "currentSellingPrice": 21000,
  "currentStock": 100
}

> {%
client.global.set("productId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get product by id
GET {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update product
PUT {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Thép phi 6 (cập nhật)",
  "unit": "kg",
  "currentImportPrice": 19000,
  "currentSellingPrice": 22000
}

### Delete product
DELETE {{host}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
